Load CHOLMOD before unpatched Eigen 3.4's extern "C" wrapper so that the CUDA
C++ declarations retain C++ linkage. CHOLMOD supplies its own C linkage
guards. Eigen removed the redundant wrapper upstream:
https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen/-/merge_requests/1561

nanoeigenpy also uses this include order in its unmerged CMake refactor:
https://github.com/Simple-Robotics/nanoeigenpy/pull/40
https://github.com/Simple-Robotics/nanoeigenpy/commit/f61c95eb50937672c648822b517ba1bb99476ab8
That commit changes fwd.hpp and relies on feature definitions from the
refactor. This workaround applies the same include order at the CHOLMOD
binding header, retaining compatibility with nanoeigenpy 0.5.0.

diff --git a/include/nanoeigenpy/decompositions/sparse/cholmod/cholmod-base.hpp b/include/nanoeigenpy/decompositions/sparse/cholmod/cholmod-base.hpp
--- a/include/nanoeigenpy/decompositions/sparse/cholmod/cholmod-base.hpp
+++ b/include/nanoeigenpy/decompositions/sparse/cholmod/cholmod-base.hpp
@@ -4,6 +4,10 @@
 
 #include "nanoeigenpy/fwd.hpp"
 #include "nanoeigenpy/decompositions/sparse/sparse-solver-base.hpp"
+// Eigen 3.4 includes cholmod.h inside extern "C". Load its CUDA C++ headers
+// before entering that block.
+#include <cholmod.h>
+
 #include <Eigen/CholmodSupport>
 
 namespace nanoeigenpy {
